    "description-s": "STM32N657X0 is a high-performance microcontroller based on the Arm Cortex-M55 32-bit RISC core operating at up to 800 MHz (overdrive), integrating an ST Neural-ART Accelerator NPU (up to 1 GHz, 600 GOPS), a Neo-Chrom 2.5D GPU, hardware H264 video encoder, JPEG codec, ISP, and 4.2-Mbyte contiguous SRAM. The device offers extensive connectivity (2x USB2.0 HS OTG, Gigabit Ethernet, 4x I2C, 2x I3C, 6x SPI, 2x SAI, 5x USART/5x UART+LPUART, 2x SDMMC, 3x FDCAN), a rich set of timers, dual 12-bit ADCs, camera (parallel + 2-lane CSI-2) and display (LCD-TFT) interfaces, and advanced security (TrustZone, secure boot, crypto accelerators). It is packaged in a VFBGA264 (14x14 mm, 0.8 mm pitch) package and is rated for the industrial operating temperature range of -40 to +125 °C.",
