      "io_voltage_mv_i": 3300,
      "clock_note-s": "HSE 25 MHz crystal (DS14791 Table 37: 16-48 MHz, Gmcritmax 1.95 mA/V, 4 pF stray): HSI is 64 MHz +-0.5 % at 30 C but drifts +-5 % over -40..125 C (DS14791 Table 43), too loose for USB HS, UART boot and audio sample rates. 25 MHz shares the MAX96716 crystal (ECS-250-8-33-JGN-TR, 8 pF, 40 ohm, C0 5 pF: gm about 0.67 mA/V). 50 ppm is this row's choice, not an ST figure.",
      "smps_note_s": "VFBSMPS: SMPS feedback, on VCORE (VDDCORE). DS14791 Rev 2 section 3.4.4 p22: 'The SMPS generates this voltage on VLXSMPS, with a total external capacitor of 88 (4x 22) uF (typical). The SMPS requires an external coil of 1 uH (typical).' Figure 2 'SMPS supply' drawing: VDDSMPS and VDDA18PMU on VDD18, VLXSMPS through the coil to VCORE/VDDCORE, VFBSMPS on VCORE. Internal SMPS on (Raul, 2026-10-17). | VDDCORE: 4 x 22 uF for the internal SMPS output ('total external capacitor of 88 (4x 22) uF'). DS14791 Rev 2 section 3.4.4 p22: 'The SMPS generates this voltage on VLXSMPS, with a total external capacitor of 88 (4x 22) uF (typical). The SMPS requires an external coil of 1 uH (typical).' Figure 2 'SMPS supply' drawing: VDDSMPS and VDDA18PMU on VDD18, VLXSMPS through the coil to VCORE/VDDCORE, VFBSMPS on VCORE. Internal SMPS on (Raul, 2026-10-17). | VDDCSI on VCORE: AN5967 Rev 2 p6, 'Note: VDDCSI must be connected to VDDCORE as 0.8 V typical power.'",
      "decoupling_note_s": "AN5967 Rev 2 Table 4 (p7): VDD, VDDIO2-5 n x 100 nF; VBAT 100 nF (VBAT on its own 3.3 V rail, not VDD); VDD33USB 1 uF; VDDA18PMU/CSI/USB/ADC/AON/PLL 100 nF each; VDDSMPS 2 x 10 uF + 2 x 1 uF + 2 x 100 nF; VLXSMPS 1 uH coil to VDDCORE + 2.2 nF to VSS; V08CAP 4.7 uF; VREF+ 1 uF + 100 nF to VSSA; VDDCORE n x 1 uF plus the SMPS output bulk 4 x 22 uF (DS14791 3.4.4; AN5967 gives 4 x 15 uF), one per ball; VDDCSI 1 uF"
    },
    "pinmux-note-s": "boot-pins-ao (2026-10-17): the STM32N6 has no internal flash and boots from the NOR on XSPIM_P2 (DS14791 marks XSPIM_P2_NCS1 / IO0 / DQS0 '(boot)'), whatever this SKU's mux; BOOT0 (G4) / BOOT1 (PA6, P8) straps and SWD (PA13, PA14) are kept free too.",
